WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.450
Here's Jeeves, an open source app for productivity workflows.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.250
Build a process once and use it again.

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:11.002
This workflow sorts incoming requests.

00:00:11.392 --> 00:00:15.202
Each agent has a job, and you can open any step to see what happened.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.110
Jev recognizes an outage and sends it to the incident agent.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:24.230
The decision shows its answer, confidence, and chosen route.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.910
When a request is missing details, Jeeves will ask you a question.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.570
The workflow saves its progress and waits until you answer.

00:00:34.852 --> 00:00:36.782
Add the details and submit.

00:00:37.152 --> 00:00:38.862
The workflow picks up from where it stopped.

00:00:40.124 --> 00:00:45.034
Now you have an action brief, a suggested fix, and a draft reply to review.

00:00:45.404 --> 00:00:47.014
Nothing has been sent to the customer.

00:00:50.124 --> 00:00:55.094
Save this workflow for the next request, or export it as a skill to use elsewhere.

00:00:57.124 --> 00:00:59.334
Try Jeeves at get Jeeves dot app.

00:00:59.464 --> 00:01:02.894
Start with the built-in example, no API key needed.

